{
  "dom_id": "step-e4390",
  "name": "Example: Identifying a Zero Matrix",
  "problem": "Which of the following are zero matrices?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "- $P$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a zero matrix since some of its entries are not zeros (for instance, $q_{12}=0.1\\neq0$).\n\n- $R$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $R$ are zero matrices.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
